## What was made available to Data Science (never claimed back)
- Validated, multivariate-confirmed risk-driver ranking (lead time, prior no-shows, distance, reminder status).
- Effect-size ranking (Cramér's V).
- Refined reminder-channel finding (SMS vs. WhatsApp, statistically significant; SMS vs. Email, inconclusive).
- A cross-validated model benchmark (Logistic Regression, 66.0% ± 1.9% recall) to compare any independently-built model against.

## What was never received
- Confirmation of which features Data Science used in their own model.
- Data Science's model performance on the Data Analytics-defined high-risk segment.
- Data Science's feature-importance ranking.

## Resolution for final submission
Since no counterpart model was ever provided, the self-built, cross-validated Logistic Regression model stands as the final predictive component for this track's contribution, clearly labelled throughout as self-built rather than the product of genuine two-way cross-track collaboration. This is reported factually in the Week 8 Final Integration Package and in the individual presentation video, rather than represented as a completed integration.

## Other tracks (Project Management, ML Engineering, GenAI)
No outreach was attempted with these tracks, as no dependency requiring their input was identified for the Data Analytics track's Week 8 deliverable. Their potential future integration points are noted as open opportunities in the End-to-End Integration Walkthrough (Section 5–7), not as attempted-and-failed dependencies.
